---The array-map processor transforms each element of a source array by applying
---sub-processors in order and collecting the results into a target array.
---Results can be written to a new array, to the source array (in-place), or to
---an existing target array. Sub-processors can read from `$sourceElem.<field>`
---(object element field), bare `$sourceElem` (primitive element), or any parent
---log attribute path. Sub-processors write to `$targetElem.<field>` (object
---output field) or bare `$targetElem` (primitive output).
---@class datadog.v1.LogsArrayMapProcessor
---@field is_enabled? boolean Whether or not the processor is enabled.
---@field name? string Name of the processor.
---@field preserve_source? boolean When `false` and `source != target`, the source attribute is removed after processing. Cannot be `false` when `source == target`.
---@field processors datadog.v1.LogsArrayMapProcessorProcessorsList Sub-processors applied to each element. Allowed types: `attribute-remapper`, `string-builder-processor`, `arithmetic-processor`, `category-processor`.
---@field source string Attribute path of the source array. Elements are read-only via `$sourceElem` inside sub-processors.
---@field target string Attribute path of the output array. Sub-processors write to `$targetElem` (or `$targetElem.<field>`) to build each output element.
---@field type datadog.v1.LogsArrayMapProcessorType|string

---Sub-processors applied to each element. Allowed types: `attribute-remapper`,
