---An object that holds an SLI value and its associated data. It can represent an SLO's overall SLI value.
---This can also represent the SLI value for a specific monitor in multi-monitor SLOs, or a group in grouped SLOs.
---@class datadog.v1.SLOHistoryMonitor
---@field error_budget_remaining? datadog.v1.SLOErrorBudgetRemainingData
---@field errors? datadog.v1.SLOHistoryMonitorErrorsList An array of error objects returned while querying the history data for the service level objective.
---@field group? string For groups in a grouped SLO, this is the group name.
---@field history? datadog.v1.SLOHistoryMonitorHistoryList The state transition history for the monitor. It is represented as an array of pairs. Each pair is an array containing the timestamp of the transition as an integer in Unix epoch format in the first element, and the state as an integer in the second element. An integer value of `0` for state means uptime, `1` means downtime, and `2` means no data. Periods of no data are counted either as uptime or downtime depending on monitor settings. See [SLO documentation](https://docs.datadoghq.com/service_management/service_level_objectives/monitor/#missing-data) for detailed information.
---@field monitor_modified? number For `monitor` based SLOs, this is the last modified timestamp in epoch seconds of the monitor.
---@field monitor_type? string For `monitor` based SLOs, this describes the type of monitor.
---@field name? string For groups in a grouped SLO, this is the group name. For monitors in a multi-monitor SLO, this is the monitor name.
---@field precision? number The amount of decimal places the SLI value is accurate to for the given from `&&` to timestamp. Use `span_precision` instead.
---@field preview? boolean For `monitor` based SLOs, when `true` this indicates that a replay is in progress to give an accurate uptime calculation.
---@field sli_value? number|distilled.Null The current SLI value of the SLO over the history window.
---@field span_precision? number The amount of decimal places the SLI value is accurate to for the given from `&&` to timestamp.
---@field uptime? number Use `sli_value` instead.

---An array of error objects returned while querying the history data for the service level objective.
---@alias datadog.v1.SLOHistoryMonitorErrorsList datadog.v1.SLOHistoryResponseErrorWithType[]

